            <div xml:id="d59">

                <pb facs="0170" n="76" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg76"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00 R 296/700: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-11-16T15:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 16,
                                1924—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 3:10 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>174. Your no. 130, November 6, 5 p.m.<anchor n="72" xml:id="d59-f1"/> I
                    understand that the Secretary General of the Italian Foreign Office has stated
                    that he sees no reason why Italian delegation should not support American
                    position for payment of claims. I have advised Logan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
